## Content Guidelines

- Document **this section only** (even inside a range). Do not mix in the next/previous chapter.
- Preserve the site’s explanations, examples, exercises, tables, and warnings. Rewrite for study; do not paste ads, nav chrome, or cookie banners.
- **Be thorough.** Every Tryit, every reference-table row, and every named construct gets its own `### Example` block with explanation, tested code, code snap, result snap, and a written outcome. Add extra examples when they clarify a concept. A bullet list of method names is **not** coverage.
- **Self-check before filing:** count Tryits + table rows + named constructs on the page; count `### **Example` headings in the course file; count Introduction **Example N:** lines with a `[View](#<slug>-example-NN)` link. All three must agree. If the Introduction omits any title or View link, or an example heading is missing its `<a id="…">`, you are not done. Do not file the section.
- Terminal Commands = only commands you actually used (`node`, `npm install`, server, open URL). If none, keep the child with a one-line placeholder.
- Fenced code is the **tested** sandbox source. If you updated outdated snippets, fence what actually ran and say how it differs from the page.
- If a snap file is missing, do not fake an `<img>` path. Finish the snaps first.

